# Your fork is where you actually study, so these are the files that fill with your own life:
# your faith profile, your running plans and sessions, and your journal entries. None of it
# should ever reach a commit. The leading slash anchors each pattern to the top level, so the
# invented worked example under example/ is still committed. Delete these lines only if you are
# certain you want your prayer journal in version control.
/profile.md
/state/
/journal/

# templates/ and example/ ARE committed. They carry no real data: the example is an invented
# person, and the templates are empty shapes.

.DS_Store
